WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:03.949
Her son would be avenged.

00:00:03.949 --> 00:00:08.059
Whispers slithered through the taverns and
back alleys of Flea Bottom.

00:00:08.059 --> 00:00:15.030
Two men were found; one was a former gold
cloak, the other a rat catcher in the Red

00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:17.870
Keep who knew all its secrets.

00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:22.840
History remembers them only as Blood and Cheese.

00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:27.230
One night, Queen Helaena entered the royal
apartments with her daughter and two sons

00:00:27.230 --> 00:00:28.940
to put them to bed.

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:33.410
Without warning, Blood and Cheese burst in,
daggers in hand.

00:00:33.410 --> 00:00:35.690
They told her that a debt was owed.

00:00:35.690 --> 00:00:38.070
A son for a son.

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:42.860
Blood and Cheese demanded she choose which
son would be ripped from her forever.

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:47.870
Queen Helaena pleaded with the men to kill
her instead, but they refused.

00:00:47.870 --> 00:00:52.730
Weeping, Helaena named her younger son Maelor.

00:00:52.730 --> 00:00:58.140
Perhaps she thought the boy was too young
to understand, perhaps because the older boy

00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:01.690
was King Aegon's firstborn son and heir.

00:01:01.690 --> 00:01:04.300
"You hear that, little boy?"

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:06.820
Cheese whispered to the younger son.

00:01:06.820 --> 00:01:10.270
"Your mama wants you dead."

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:14.460
Then Blood struck off the older boy's head
with a single blow.

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:19.600
When the guards burst in, they found Queen
Helaena still screaming, clasping her dead

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:23.260
son's body to her, mad with grief.

00:01:23.260 --> 00:02:09.440
The blood of her children transformed a dynastic
dispute into a war 

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:14.020
of annihilation.

00:02:14.020 --> 00:02:21.360
The grief and rage of losing a child could
burn down the world.

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:26.330
Either Aegon or Rhaenyra could live at the
end, but not both.

00:02:26.330 --> 00:02:31.350
Viserys: Rhaenyra's forces struck yet another
blow.

00:02:31.350 --> 00:02:35.800
The moment the Lord of Harrenhal saw Daemon
Targaryen circling the castle on his dragon

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:39.130
Caraxes, he struck his banners and surrendered.

00:02:39.130 --> 00:02:42.690
The Blacks now had the strongest castle in
the Riverlands.

00:02:42.690 --> 00:02:48.110
Darker news still came to Aegon; thanks to
Rhaenyra's sons, Winterfell had declared for

00:02:48.110 --> 00:02:50.800
Rhaenyra, as had the Vale.

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:55.001
Furious, Aegon dismissed his grandfather,
Ser Otto, as Hand and appointed Ser Criston

00:02:55.001 --> 00:02:59.730
Cole, who swore to march on all the lords
who had declared for Rhaenyra and put their

00:02:59.730 --> 00:03:00.909
castles to the torch.

00:03:00.909 --> 00:03:06.920
Cole and the royal army first marched north
and laid siege to Rook's Rest, a Black stronghold

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:08.200
near Dragonstone.

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:12.710
When the Lord saw their approach, he sent
a raven to Rhaenyra begging for help.

00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:18.130
For days he watched his fields and villages
burning, with no response from his queen.

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:22.120
Until one day, a shadow passed over the Green
army.

00:03:22.120 --> 00:03:28.310
Rhaenyra had sent not an army, but her former
mother-by-law Rhaenys and her dragon Meleys.

00:03:28.310 --> 00:03:33.439
As her ancestor had done at the Field of Fire,
Rhaenys gleefully began to incinerate Ser

00:03:33.439 --> 00:03:34.439
Criston's army.

00:03:34.439 --> 00:03:38.860
But Aegon had set a trap, and Rhaenys had
flown right into it.

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:44.590
As Rhaenys and Meleys blanketed Ser Criston's
troops in dragonflame, two other dragons rose

00:03:44.590 --> 00:03:45.930
into the sky.

00:03:45.930 --> 00:03:50.290
Aemond on Vhagar and King Aegon himself on
the gleaming Sunfyre.

00:03:50.290 --> 00:03:54.689
To her credit, Rhaenys didn't flee.

00:03:54.689 --> 00:03:59.770
Dragon fought dragons, and a second sun blossomed
in the sky.

00:03:59.770 --> 00:04:03.500
When the smoke cleared, only Aemond and Vhagar
stood uninjured.

00:04:03.500 --> 00:04:08.140
Sunfyre, the most magnificent dragon in the
world, had one of its wings almost completely

00:04:08.140 --> 00:04:10.189
torn from its body.

00:04:10.189 --> 00:04:15.110
Trapped beneath Sunfyre was the king himself,
broken and burned so badly in places that

00:04:15.110 --> 00:04:18.229
his armor had fused onto his flesh.

00:04:18.229 --> 00:04:22.229
His body survived, but his mind was given
over to milk of the poppy.

00:04:22.229 --> 00:04:29.900
Meleys had been torn to shreds, and her rider,
Rhaenys, was a pile of ash.

00:04:29.900 --> 00:04:34.510
Panicked by the defeat, Rhaenyra shipped her
two youngest sons across the Narrow Sea for

00:04:34.510 --> 00:04:35.510
their protection.

00:04:35.510 --> 00:04:40.570
Only for her youngest to return days later,
clinging to the neck of his wounded and dying

00:04:40.570 --> 00:04:41.570
dragon.

00:04:41.570 --> 00:04:45.740
He and his brother had been set upon by an
enemy fleet just off Dragonstone.

00:04:45.740 --> 00:04:50.860
Defying his mother's command, Rhaenyra's eldest
son and heir, Jacaerys, mounted his dragon

00:04:50.860 --> 00:04:54.470
Vermaxand flew to rescue his other brother
and punish the enemy fleet.

00:04:54.470 --> 00:05:01.000
But the foolish boy let Vermax be hooked like
a trout and dragged into the sea, where he

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:03.910
soaked up even more arrows than seawater.

00:05:03.910 --> 00:05:08.360
His brother disappeared over the horizon or
beneath the waves.

00:05:08.360 --> 00:05:09.800
No one could say for sure.

00:05:09.800 --> 00:05:14.350
With the loss of four dragons, Rhaenyra's
only advantage was fading.

00:05:14.350 --> 00:05:20.190
Luckily for her, over the centuries, House
Targaryen had spilled more than blood on Dragonstone.

00:05:20.190 --> 00:05:24.800
She promised gold and title to any of the
Targaryen bastards who could tame the six

00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:27.130
untamed dragons on the island.

00:05:27.130 --> 00:05:32.440
These bastards were called the dragonseeds,
though most were called supper.

00:05:32.440 --> 00:05:37.310
Perhaps the dragons were eventually sated
or bored, but four of them accepted riders

00:05:37.310 --> 00:05:39.949
and were enlisted in Rhaenyra's cause.

00:05:39.949 --> 00:05:44.979
Robert: After Rook's Rest, Aemond One-Eye
took command of the Greens from his crippled

00:05:44.979 --> 00:05:46.860
and poppy-addled brother.

00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:52.060
Aemond was the blood of the dragon, and dragons
don't cower behind city walls.

00:05:52.060 --> 00:05:57.759
He marched the king's army north to take back
Harrenhal from Rhaenyra's husband, Daemon.

00:05:57.759 --> 00:06:03.729
But when he and Criston Cole reached the castle,
they found the gates open, with Daemon and

00:06:03.729 --> 00:06:05.979
all his men gone.

00:06:05.979 --> 00:06:12.060
That night they feasted their victory; Daemon
had fled rather than face their wrath.

00:06:12.060 --> 00:06:15.759
But Daemon was more snake than dragon.

00:06:15.759 --> 00:06:22.099
As Aemond marched north, he'd flown Caraxes
south, slithering past the Green army over

00:06:22.099 --> 00:06:24.530
the waters of the Gods Eye.

00:06:24.530 --> 00:06:29.830
One day King's Landing looked up and saw two
dragons circling their foul city.

00:06:29.830 --> 00:06:35.810
Daemon and Rhaenyra had come for her throne,
for the city was defenseless.

00:06:35.810 --> 00:06:42.970
Aemond had taken the king's army from the
city, and worse, he'd taken his dragon Vhagar.

00:06:42.970 --> 00:06:48.540
Seeing that resistance was hopeless, the small
council surrendered the city, the Queen Mother

00:06:48.540 --> 00:06:52.310
Alicent, and the broken Queen Helaena.

00:06:52.310 --> 00:06:54.319
But not King Aegon.

00:06:54.319 --> 00:07:00.400
Somehow, despite his wounds and delirium,
he had vanished from the city.

00:07:00.400 --> 00:07:06.330
And so Queen Rhaenyra climbed the steps and
seated herself of the Iron Throne.

00:07:06.330 --> 00:07:12.259
Legend has it that as she left that hall later,
blood trickled down her legs and hands, proving

00:07:12.259 --> 00:07:15.940
the Iron Throne had spurned her.

00:07:15.940 --> 00:07:16.940
Nonsense!

00:07:16.940 --> 00:07:19.650
It's a chair made of steel blades.

00:07:19.650 --> 00:07:24.960
Rhaenyra had wanted it all her life and had
sacrificed two sons for it.

00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:28.139
She likely gripped the damn thing too tight.

00:07:28.139 --> 00:07:34.560
Viserys: When Aemond realized that his arrogance
had cost him the capital, he mounted Vhagar

00:07:34.560 --> 00:07:40.810
in a black rage and rained fire onto every
village and castle he suspected of disloyalty.

00:07:40.810 --> 00:07:45.150
Abandoned by Aemond, Ser Criston marched the
royal army back to King's Landing, intent

00:07:45.150 --> 00:07:47.150
on recapturing the city himself.

00:07:47.150 --> 00:07:51.889
Instead, he was trapped and cut to pieces
by the Riverlords, who had sworn to support

00:07:51.889 --> 00:07:52.889
Rhaenyra's claim.

00:07:52.889 --> 00:07:58.020
When a new army of Green loyalists marched
up from the Reach and laid siege to the city

00:07:58.020 --> 00:08:02.740
of Tumbleton, Rhaenyra sent two of her dragonseeds
to lay waste to them.

00:08:02.740 --> 00:08:07.050
Instead, the dragonseeds proved their bastard
nature and betrayed her.

00:08:07.050 --> 00:08:11.780
They burned the city and all the Black forces
garrisoned within.

00:08:11.780 --> 00:08:16.080
Lucky for her, they didn't turn towards King's
Landing but whored and drank in the ruins

00:08:16.080 --> 00:08:20.320
with the Greens, who were victorious and somewhat
confused.

00:08:20.320 --> 00:08:26.340
Oberyn Martell: Rhaenyra now mistrusted all
the dragonseeds, including the girl who rode

00:08:26.340 --> 00:08:30.980
with her husband Daemon, hunting Aemond in
the Riverlands.

00:08:30.980 --> 00:08:33.919
She ordered the girl's head be sent to her.

00:08:33.919 --> 00:08:38.289
But there was a complication.

00:08:38.289 --> 00:08:42.669
As well as her dragon, the girl had taken
to riding Daemon.

00:08:42.669 --> 00:08:46.959
When Daemon received the queen's order, he
proclaimed it a queen's words and a whore's

00:08:46.959 --> 00:08:47.959
work.

00:08:47.959 --> 00:08:53.230
He sent the girl away at dawn, watching her
and her dragon vanish into the morning mists.

00:08:53.230 --> 00:09:01.350
Then Daemon sent a challenge to his nephew
Aemond and flew to Harrenhal alone to wait.

00:09:01.350 --> 00:09:06.690
Fourteen days later, a shadow blacker than
any passing cloud swept over Harrenhal.

00:09:06.690 --> 00:09:12.829
Vhagar had come at last and on her rode one-eyed
Prince Aemond.

00:09:12.829 --> 00:09:14.810
He mocked Daemon for facing him alone.

00:09:14.810 --> 00:09:16.920
"You have lived too long, uncle."

00:09:16.920 --> 00:09:21.430
And Daemon replied, "On that much, we agree."

00:09:21.430 --> 00:09:26.610
Then the old prince climbed stiffly onto the
back of his dragon Caraxes but neglected to

00:09:26.610 --> 00:09:30.089
fasten the chains that secured rider to saddle.

00:09:30.089 --> 00:09:35.790
The sun was close to setting when, as one,
the two dragons leapt into the sky.

00:09:35.790 --> 00:09:39.660
Daemon took Caraxes up swiftly until he disappeared
into a bank of clouds.

00:09:39.660 --> 00:09:43.079
Vhagar, older and slower, ascended more gradually.

00:09:43.079 --> 00:09:47.529
Up and up, Vhagar soared, searching for Caraxes.

00:09:47.529 --> 00:09:51.519
Sudden as a thunderbolt, a shrieking Caraxes
dove upon Vhagar.

00:09:51.519 --> 00:09:54.570
Locked together, the dragons tumbled toward
the lake.

00:09:54.570 --> 00:09:59.350
Caraxes' jaws closed upon Vhagar's neck, but
Vhagar ripped open Caraxes's belly, and her

00:09:59.350 --> 00:10:01.440
teeth ripped off a wing.

00:10:01.440 --> 00:10:04.420
The lake rushed up with terrible speed.

00:10:04.420 --> 00:10:10.430
Then Daemon Targaryen, who had never fastened
his riding chains, stood in his saddle.

00:10:10.430 --> 00:10:15.940
He leapt from his dragon to Aemond's, and
in his hand was Dark Sister, the Valyrian

00:10:15.940 --> 00:10:19.180
sword of Aegon's sister-queen Visenya.

00:10:19.180 --> 00:10:24.300
As Aemond One-Eye looked up in terror, Daemon
ripped off his nephew's helm and drove the

00:10:24.300 --> 00:10:30.370
sword down into his one remaining eye so hard
the point came out the back of the young prince's

00:10:30.370 --> 00:10:31.370
throat.

00:10:31.370 --> 00:10:36.899
Half a heartbeat later, the dragons struck
the lake, sending up a gout of water so high

00:10:36.899 --> 00:10:41.350
that it was said to have been as tall as Harrenhal's
great tower.

00:10:41.350 --> 00:10:48.050
The lake boiled with dragon blood and then
was still.

00:10:48.050 --> 00:10:51.710
Daemon Targaryen was nine-and-forty at his
death.

00:10:51.710 --> 00:10:54.500
Prince Aemond had only turned twenty.

00:10:54.500 --> 00:11:02.860
Vhagar, the greatest of the Targaryen dragons,
had counted one-hundred-and-eighty-one years.

00:11:02.860 --> 00:11:07.320
Thus passed the last living creature from
the days of Aegon's Conquest.

00:11:07.320 --> 00:11:13.570
Viserys: Back in King's Landing, Queen Rhaenyra
didn't have much time to grieve for her stupid

00:11:13.570 --> 00:11:14.570
husband.

00:11:14.570 --> 00:11:19.000
The mad former queen Helaena flung herself
from a balcony, to be impaled upon the iron

00:11:19.000 --> 00:11:21.980
spikes lining the moat of Maegor's Holdfast.

00:11:21.980 --> 00:11:27.660
That night, the city rose in riot against
Rhaenyra, demanding justice for Queen Helaena

00:11:27.660 --> 00:11:32.320
and her murdered son, among other foolish
peasantfantasies.

00:11:32.320 --> 00:11:37.590
In the midst of this chaos, a one-handed fool
called the Shepherd began to rant against

00:11:37.590 --> 00:11:38.590
dragons.

00:11:38.590 --> 00:11:41.390
Not just the ones of the enemy, but all dragons
everywhere.

00:11:41.390 --> 00:11:47.660
As he pointed to the Dragonpit above on the
hill, he shouted, "There the demons dwell,

00:11:47.660 --> 00:11:48.660
this is their city.

00:11:48.660 --> 00:11:52.190
If you would make it yours, first you must
destroy them."

00:11:52.190 --> 00:11:56.930
A cry went up from ten thousand throats, "Kill
them!"

00:11:56.930 --> 00:12:00.839
There were four dragons housed within the
Dragonpit that night.

00:12:00.839 --> 00:12:06.970
By the time the first of the attackers came
pouring in, all four were roused, awake and

00:12:06.970 --> 00:12:07.970
angry.

00:12:07.970 --> 00:12:10.610
Nobody knows how many men and women died that
night.

00:12:10.610 --> 00:12:11.610
Who cares?

00:12:11.610 --> 00:12:13.190
They all should have!

00:12:13.190 --> 00:12:15.769
Trapped within the pit, the dragons could
not fly.

00:12:15.769 --> 00:12:19.910
Instead, they fought with horns, claws, teeth,
and fire.

00:12:19.910 --> 00:12:25.560
For every man who died, ten more appeared,
shouting that the dragons must die.

00:12:25.560 --> 00:12:28.210
One by one, they did.

00:12:28.210 --> 00:12:32.540
Finally, the last remaining dragon broke her
chain, spread her wings, and flew straight

00:12:32.540 --> 00:12:34.930
up at the great dome trying to flee.

00:12:34.930 --> 00:12:39.970
Already weakened by dragonflame, the dome
cracked under the force of impact and then

00:12:39.970 --> 00:12:44.540
tumbled down, crushing the dragonslayers and
herself.

00:12:44.540 --> 00:12:49.820
Joffrey Baratheon: High atop the Red Keep,
Queen Rhaenyra clutched her two remaining

00:12:49.820 --> 00:12:55.870
sons to her as she watched the end of her
family's might, too afraid of the peasants

00:12:55.870 --> 00:12:57.790
to defend her dragons.

00:12:57.790 --> 00:13:01.889
At least her older son, Joffrey, had a man's
spine.

00:13:01.889 --> 00:13:07.180
He stole his mother's dragon Syrax and tried
to fly it to the Dragonpit to save his birthright.

00:13:07.180 --> 00:13:13.399
But the stupid beast didn't understand and
twisted beneath him, fighting to be free of

00:13:13.399 --> 00:13:17.710
the little boy, until it was.

00:13:17.710 --> 00:13:23.699
A queen is still a woman, with all the weakness
of that sex.

00:13:23.699 --> 00:13:29.570
Weeping for her lost son more than her dragons,
Rhaenyra abandoned the Iron Throne and sold

00:13:29.570 --> 00:13:34.829
her crown to buy passage for her and her last
son back to Dragonstone.

00:13:34.829 --> 00:13:39.320
Rhaenyra hoped to hatch more dragons from
the eggs in the castle.

00:13:39.320 --> 00:13:44.750
But when she landed, the welcoming party slew
her guards and marched her and her son at

00:13:44.750 --> 00:13:50.769
spearpoint to the castle to face a dead man
and a dying dragon.

00:13:50.769 --> 00:13:51.949
"Sister!"

00:13:51.949 --> 00:13:55.490
King Aegon, Second of His Name, called out
to Rhaenyra.

00:13:55.490 --> 00:14:02.399
Rook's Rest had left Aegon bent and twisted,
his once handsome face puffy from milk of

00:14:02.399 --> 00:14:06.760
the poppy, with burn scars covering half his
body.

00:14:06.760 --> 00:14:12.200
Rhaenyra, ever defiant, told her dear brother
that she'd hoped he was dead.

00:14:12.200 --> 00:14:14.240
"After you!"

00:14:14.240 --> 00:14:16.279
Aegon answered.

00:14:16.279 --> 00:14:26.779
Then Sunfyre bathed her in a blast of flame
and devoured her in six bites while her son

00:14:26.779 --> 00:14:34.589
watched, leaving the seventh and final bite,
her lower leg, for the Stranger.

00:14:34.589 --> 00:14:40.959
Viserys: Rhaenyra was dead, and King Aegon
sat the Iron Throne again.

00:14:40.959 --> 00:14:43.709
But only for half a year.

00:14:43.709 --> 00:14:48.050
He was poisoned by his own men and replaced
with the very boy who had watched his mother

00:14:48.050 --> 00:14:49.440
devoured.

00:14:49.440 --> 00:14:56.170
Shireen: When Rhaenyra's last son wed Aegon's
only daughter, the Dance of Dragons officially

00:14:56.170 --> 00:14:57.170
ended.

00:14:57.170 --> 00:14:59.470
Ash and burned men.

00:14:59.470 --> 00:15:02.980
All that was left of the Riverlands.

00:15:02.980 --> 00:15:06.100
Two scared children spouting oaths they didn't
understand.

00:15:06.100 --> 00:15:10.060
All that was left of the mighty House Targaryen.

00:15:10.060 --> 00:15:25.310
Ancient skulls and hatchlings that grew no
bigger than cats.

00:15:25.310 --> 00:15:46.239
All that was left of the dragons.

